  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "Executable Candidate recipe of NVIDIA's DGX Spark playbook (vllm) for Llama 3.1 405B Instruct AWQ INT4: vllm 0.21.0+2325b6f0 (NVIDIA NGC vllm 26.05.post1-py3), pinned by arm64 digest, serving the exact model revision through `vllm serve` with the playbook's flags (vLLM defaults where the playbook passes none). Tensor parallel 4 across four Sparks uses vLLM's native multi-node launch (the platform's --nnodes/--node-rank placement options) instead of the playbook's hand-started Ray cluster: the pinned NVIDIA NGC vllm 26.05.post1 image does not ship Ray (its layers hold no ray package and no ray executable), and vLLM rejects --nnodes with the Ray executor. Deviation from the playbook: the context is 512 tokens (batched tokens 512) instead of 64, so the sweep's 256-token A323 chat case plus its prompt fits the context and the bounded 64-token chat check fits too. Four Sparks, not two: the AWQ INT4 checkpoint is 204.22 GiB, so a pair holds 109.64 GB of weights per rank against about 119.4 GiB usable. Hardware-observed 2026-11-01 (two Sparks, tensor parallel 2): both ranks ran out of memory during weight loading (the host guard killed the worker on one Spark at MemAvailable 0; the kernel OOM-killed the other), and swap stayed unused because the weights land in GPU/driver memory. NVIDIA's own playbook notes insufficient memory headroom on two Sparks and marks that setup testing only. At tensor parallel 4 (128 attention heads and 16 KV heads divide evenly) each rank holds about 54.8 GB of weights. Per-rank peak is the honest loading floor: 54,821,967,093 bytes of weights (219,287,868,370 / 4, rounded up) plus the 1,073,741,824-byte KV pool plus the 8,000,000,000-byte runtime-overhead estimate; it is an offline estimate, not a measurement, and physical acceptance is pending. The explicit KV pool of 1,073,741,824 bytes per rank holds 4,161 tokens at 258,048 bytes/token (126 layers x 4 KV heads per TP=4 rank x 128 head_dim x 2 K/V x 2 bytes), eight full-context requests at the 512-token context; utilization 0.48 (62.7 GB) is only vLLM's startup free-memory check beside the fixed pool and must stay at or below the per-rank peak; the playbook's 0.85 would require 111 GB free per rank, which no honest four-rank peak declares. It needs four enrolled Sparks.",
